title A guard met a birth -- the reach gate read one past both ceilings, and the Mac bench paid the debt named for it
prompt The SILENCE seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves; pick up the running thread and take the next infrastructure lap.
think Rota N=3722 by git rev-list --count HEAD, row 2 -- fire, Mars, cut and stop, the row that SEES. Read the threshold, Standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. The row advanced by exactly one from the prior lap's row 1, so no hand-advance was owed. Its cardinal seat chose the lap: the eye refuses to look away from a known wrong, and the roster had one.
think The cold roster took 46 minutes and closed 92 guards, 87 green, 5 red, tree_moved=no. I held every write until it finished, and held rye build too -- the Caravan suite was building while I read, and REDS %281 is two concurrent builds deleting each other's .zig shadows.
think witness_reach was the one red in my lane: unreached=1109 against ceiling=1108 and wholly_unreached=221 against family_ceiling=220, both exactly one over, which is a ratchet meeting a birth rather than a new class of fault. `witness_reach_scan.sh --families` named the root without guessing: two singleton families reading 100% unreached, `macos` and `ios`.
think The scan's own ceiling comment had already written half the answer a day earlier -- tools/m/macos_app_bundle_witness.rish "CANNOT take a clock on this pier ... its row belongs to the lane that can run it GREEN on a Mac before promising it." This is that Mac bench. The other singleton, tools/m/ios_app_shell_witness.rish, landed at 20260829.095045 from the LOCA arc and is what pushed both readings over.
think Ran tools/m/macos_app_bundle_witness.rish on metal before promising anything: GREEN in 4s, both legs -- the plist-stripped copy refused by `open -W`, the whole bundle opened through LaunchServices, receipt mode=bundle window=5308 main_menu_items=1 from a process that never had a terminal. Then one roster record in construction/standing-equipment.kyri: guard macos_app_bundle, path tools/m/macos_app_bundle_witness.rish, tier cadence, host macos, seated 20260829.104233 -- cadence and host copied from its seated macOS-surface sibling skate_native_core rather than invented.
think Declined to roster the iOS sibling, and wrote the reason into the scan's ceiling comment rather than a number: its precondition is a BOOTED SIMULATOR, which is machine state a reboot clears, where `host macos` answers what kind of machine this is. The seated tiers spell lap, cadence, and host; none spells "when a device is booted". Rostered, it would red on every lap where nobody had booted one, and a guard that reds on ordinary work is a guard somebody turns off. A simulator happens to be booted on this bench right now, left over from the 09:30 lap, which is exactly why it is state rather than a fact about the host.
obs The ceiling STANDS at 1108 rather than falling, and that is the honest reading rather than a dodge: the fall the macOS repair earned is exactly spent by the iOS birth. The scan's own file already refuses to absorb one lane's overage into another's slack -- it says so three paragraphs up about the Comlink rows -- so both facts are written there in full: the debt paid, and the debt declined with its reason.
obs The peer was named before a file moved, per REDS %291's law: ListAgents showed grain-65, and I sent it the whole intended diff before touching either file, including the offer to stop at the macos row. Naming was not enough, and that is this lap's second finding.
think While the HOT roster ran, grain-65 landed two commits -- afc8e2bed (the %334 one-hop repair) and d0b399e4c (LOCA touch input). The run closed tree_moved=yes with an extra red, reds_fold, which the cold pass had read green. It is the mid-run tree rather than a fault: tools/fixtures/r/readme_reach_scan.sh re-run after their commits reads verdict=ok and broken_in_living=0, and tools/r/reds_fold_witness.rish is GREEN on metal. witness_reach is GREEN against their landed tree too, at 1108/1108 and 220/220, so my repair holds across the move.
obs A LOST ROW, and it is %291 sharper than either instance already in that row. d0b399e4c added its own log 20260829-112105_the-finger-the-ring-admits.kyri and changed session-logs/date/README-index-20260829.md by exactly one line -- and that line was MINE, stamp 20260829.104233. The peer's own row never reached the shelf. I had prepended mine to that shared file and staged it; their `git add` of the same path took the file whole. A shelf index is the one file EVERY lap must write, so it is where two writers collide by construction. %291 cost duplicated work, which is loud; this cost a row, which is silent -- `log_has_a_row` read green on both roster passes, because it asks whether a log has a row rather than whether every log does.
obs Restored the peer's row above mine, newest-first, at 175 bytes, and told them by message rather than editing their commit. The ledger stays theirs to book: REDS is at 24,571 of 24,576 with 0 foldable and its expansion is Keaton's seat, so this rides in the log and the peer message rather than as a row I cannot fit.
obs Four reds stand after this lap and every one is somebody's word rather than mine: rule_twin at 39/36 is custody gate %7, and pond_enclosure_policy, pond_policy_launcher, and pond_enclosure_door are Hush's lane over this pier's own enclosure.conf, which %327 leaves at Keaton's hand.
